{"_id":"68a7360a8ec3d8323af11570","nodeId":"tC5ETtOuuUcybj1jI4CuG","roadmapSlug":"angular","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:50.309Z","description":"# Dynamic Components\n\nIn addition to using a component directly in a template, you can also dynamically render components. There are two main ways to dynamically render a component: in a template with `NgComponentOutlet`, or in your TypeScript code with `ViewContainerRef`.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Programmatically Rendering Components","url":"https://angular.dev/guide/components/programmatic-rendering","_id":"6a7f49d1cb44947debcf0e75"},{"type":"article","title":"New Input Binding for NgComponentOutlet","url":"https://medium.com/ngconf/new-input-binding-for-ngcomponentoutlet-cb18a86a739d","_id":"6a7f49d1cb44947debcf0e76"},{"type":"article","title":"Render dynamic components in Angular using ViewContainerRef","url":"https://dev.to/railsstudent/render-dynamic-components-in-angular-using-viewcontainerref-160h","_id":"6a7f49d1cb44947debcf0e77"},{"type":"video","title":"Dynamic Component in Angular (2024)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ncbftt3NWVo","_id":"6a7f49d1cb44947debcf0e78"},{"type":"video","title":"Mastering ViewContainerRef for dynamic component loading in Angular17","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ra4PITCt8m0","_id":"6a7f49d1cb44947debcf0e79"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:01:05.151Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/angular/content/tC5ETtOuuUcybj1jI4CuG.md"}